A oneof member is read where hand code tells it apart from its siblings: a
switch on the Which result naming its case constant, a comparison of the Which
result with its case constant, an assertion to its wrapper type. A default or
not-set arm reads nothing further and a wrapper literal assigned to the oneof
field only writes. A Has call of the oneof, a comparison of the Which result
with the not-set constant and a Get call of the oneof that is no operand tell no
member apart, so each reads every member of its oneof. A nested message's oneof
binds to the nested message (references-go.15, bindings.14). Generated by
protoc-gen-go v1.36.11 with the hybrid API from proto/v1/choices.proto.

